OL,3,AThe engine parts that 'fight the laws
OL,4,Aof the universe'
OL,5,
OL,6,FEvery time you fly, an extraordinary
OL,7,Ffeat of endurance occurs inside the
OL,8,Faircraft's engines.
OL,10,FHidden from view inside the sleek outer
OL,11,Fnacelle are hundreds of little turbine
OL,12,Fblades that can shrug off enormous
OL,13,Fmechanical stresses and temperatures
OL,14,Fexceeding 1,500C.
OL,16,FIt is a true engineering marvel. And
OL,17,Fthese hardy blades are not sculpted or
OL,18,Fcut from their material ` they are
OL,19,Fgrown.
OL,23,APub: 06-NovQppppppppppppppppppppppG5/19
OL,24,ANext PageBTechnologyC Nat RadioFCulture
FL,108,105,200,160,0,100
PN,11906
SC,0006
CT,25,T
PS,c000
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 2   F119A1793931489
OL,1,W5j 5Q#7!wsj#%uzj#57kj  7kjc1uz
OL,2,W//%*// //%Q % -,*,%%** %-.*,$-.*,%,. (,
OL,3,AThe engine parts that 'fight the laws
OL,4,Aof the universe'
OL,5,
OL,6,FDuring the 1960s, engineers worked out
OL,7,Fhow to take a molten metal alloy, cast
OL,8,Fit into the shape of a turbine blade,
OL,9,Fand then cool it very carefully from
OL,10,Fone end to the other over a matter of
OL,11,Fhours. A single crystal or grain of
OL,12,Fmetal alloy forms during this process
OL,13,Fof gradual, delicate solidification.
OL,23,APub: 06-NovQppppppppppppppppppppppG6/19
OL,24,ANext PageBTechnologyC Nat RadioFCulture
